            <ArticleTitle>[Interrelations between cardiac rhythm disorders and heart enlargement in patients with exertion-induced stenocardia and pain-free forms of ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>32-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Data from 24-h ECG monitoring of 137 patients with angina of effort or painless IHD were compared with respective X-ray evidence of heart enlargement. The patients were identified at an epidemiological screening for multifactorial IHD prevention among male residents of Kaunas, aged 40-59 yrs. A correlation was established between the enlargement of the cardiac volume and left compartments and the severity of arrhythmias.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
